Early-game genocide targets are somewhat situational,
in my opinion.  It probably depends at least partly on role,
perhaps also on what resistances you've acquired, and it
definitely depends on exactly how early in the game it is.
Whether the scroll is blessed could also be a factor
(especially if you don't have holy water yet).

It is for exactly this reason -- because it's so dependent
on circumstances and therefore different each game --
that I don't think early-game genocide needs to change
at all.  It's the late-game situation that needs work.
This is one reason I suggested a decaying-probability
formula for genocide success based on the number
of species that have already been wiped out.

It also might be interesting if genocide only applied
in the dungeons, i.e., if all species were "back in"
once you reach the planes.  But that's less of a
big deal, because the planes are so short (only
five levels total) that you really don't have time to
get very bored, (unless maybe you insist on finding
the portals via systematic exhaustive tile-by-tile
line-by-line search of each level).


